            explanation: "Lactic-acid bacteria produce acid, lowering pH and promoting aggregation or gelation of casein. The sour taste and curd formation are connected through acidification, not a rise in pH. Biology p. 164 draws this sequence explicitly beneath the yoghurt starter pair.", sectionId: "cheese-and-yoghurt", source: { document: "biology", page: 164 }, cognitive: "understanding"
