            explanation: "A brooder provides warmth and care after hatch. The source incorrectly equates brooder with a newly hatched chick; incubation instead concerns development within the egg. Biology p. 164 supplies the terms whose distinction is tested here.", sectionId: "poultry-incubation-and-brooding", source: { document: "biology", page: 164 }, cognitive: "recall"
