            explanation: "Acetic-acid bacteria such as Acetobacter oxidize ethanol to acetic acid. Azotobacter is a different genus associated with nitrogen fixation, not a spelling variant. Biology p. 165 writes Azotobacter on the arrow, and the typed source correction makes the distinction explicit.", sectionId: "microbial-organic-acids", source: { document: "biology", page: 165 }, cognitive: "recall"
