            explanation: "Aspergillus niger is the standard industrial citric-acid producer named in Biology p. 165. The other source organisms are associated primarily with ethanol, lactic acid or dextran in these notes. Industrial production remains strain- and process-specific.", sectionId: "microbial-organic-acids", source: { document: "biology", page: 165 }, cognitive: "recall"
