            explanation: "Partial starch hydrolysis yields dextrins, whereas Leuconostoc-associated synthesis from sucrose can produce dextran. The similar names do not erase the difference between breakdown and polymer synthesis. Biology p. 165 contains the two conflicting arrows that this question resolves.", sectionId: "dextrin-and-dextran", source: { document: "biology", page: 165 }, cognitive: "understanding"
